    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a read-derived `locality` field on owners, computed from the city via the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nThe field is a pure function of the already-stored `city`, so it belongs with the other read-time derivations (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, `membershipNumber`) rather than as a persisted column or write pipeline step. Changes:\n\n- **`Locality.java`** (new, `rest.function.owner`) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper owning the fixed city\u2192region table and the `region(city)` lookup, mirroring the existing owner-domain rule helpers (`SameCity`, `CustomerCode`).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `locality(Owner)` default method delegating to `Locality.region(...)` and wired it with `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = ...)`, exactly following the pattern of the sibling derived fields.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\nThe table lives in one dedicated unit, the mapper just delegates, and no class grew a catch-all.",
